> Auto-generated by /project-context | Last updated: 2026-03-06

## Goals & Strategy
Python CLI toolset for managing the ~/Movies library (295.7GB, 532 files). Provides 5-dimension macOS tagging (status / source / content / business / project), Finder color labels via AppleScript, inventory scanning, reorganization into EDITING/_Assets and READY/ structure, and safe archiving. No deletion — all moves logged and reversible.

Owner: Elad Tzur. Manages video production assets across multiple businesses (ICF/Finance, Efrat therapy content, training videos, personal family videos, stock footage/templates).

## Architecture & Tech Stack
- **Language:** Python 3 (no external dependencies beyond stdlib + ffprobe)
- **macOS integration:** AppleScript via subprocess (Finder color labels), xattr (text tags)
- **Media scanning:** ffprobe (ffmpeg) for video metadata
- **Config:** Single source of truth in `config.py` (all rules, move plans, tag definitions)
- **Data output:** CSV + Markdown (media_inventory.csv, media_inventory.md)
- **Safety:** folder_snapshot.py (snapshot/diff/restore), move_log.csv, never rm — always move to ~/.Trash/

